  "description": "Coleslaw gets a vintage twist in this mayo-free cream slaw, with a simple cream-and-vinegar dressing that's tangy and light on the perfectly crisp cabbage. It's right at home at cookouts, potlucks, picnics, and more.",
  "notes": "Total time, including resting: 2 hr 20 min.\n\nNotes: This recipe is easiest to produce with a mandoline-style slicer, though you can also finely shred the cabbage by hand. To slice cabbages on a mandoline, split the head in half, cut out the core with the tip of a sharp chef's knife, then quarter the cabbage and slice it with the mandoline set to 1/16-inch thickness.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: The coleslaw can be refrigerated for up to 1 day before serving.",
